  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe fig8 lifts of #3824 and #3825 have one cause, and it is not in `pass_link`.\n\n- **Cause.** `level_rings::sides` splits the boundary of the cutter-centre area into ring 0 (the start side) and the walls. It used a side tolerance (`SIDE_EPS`) of 1 um. The area and the start side are two offsets, and each flattens the same round joins within 5 um (`ARC_TOL_UNITS`). On fig8, at X about +-46.5 and Y about 123.2, the band is 5 mm wide. There, two 0.117 mm stretches of the part wall read as the stock side.\n  - Inside: the wall ring had a gap at each stretch, and each gap gave a lift.\n  - Outside: the two stretches were ring 0 and were cut first. Each was reached by a lift across the part and entered by a plunge into material (the four links of #3825).\n- **Fix 1** (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/level_rings.rs`): `SIDE_EPS` is now 10 um, twice the flattening error.\n- **Fix 2** (`ring_links.rs`, `ladder_links.rs`): as #3824 asks, the pass link round a part tries `edge_route` after the straight chord. Each chord of the route gets the proof of the straight chord (`chord_proof`: certified area, no crossing of `passes` and `st.level`, each sample in air or over a cut column). The whole route is within the stay-down limit. `pass_link` records the route as a cut of the level. A lift stays only when the chord and the route both fail, and it keeps the straight chord's reason. On the cases below, this change alone changes no reading. It closes the gap that the review of #3818 found.\n\n## Readings (release)\n\n| Reading | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| fig8 Inside, lifts inside a level | 6 | 0 |\n| fig8 Outside, lifts inside a level | 12 | 3 (one short hop each level, named \"would cut uncut stock with the full tool width\") |\n| fig8 Outside, lifts across the part | 4 each level | 0 |\n| fig8 Outside, \"plunged into material\" notes (Helix and Arc entry) | 6 | 0 |\n| `flute_reach`, 10 mm flute, rapid findings | 9 | 3 |\n| clamp case (`pass_start_levels::ring_links::lift_reason_is_named`), Inside / Outside lifts | 3 / 26 | 4 / 26, each named |\n\nThe clamp case: its Inside pass start (-3.29, 15.66) is where the clamp's rounded keep-out meets the part ring almost at a tangent. The meeting point moves by micrometres with the side tolerance (2 lifts at 2 um, 4 lifts from 3 um to 10 um). The decision file records this.\n\n\"Before\" for fig8 is the run with only Fix 2 in place: Inside 6, Outside 12, the same 18 lifts (9 crossing, 9 area) that #3824 reports, and the six plunge notes of #3825.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `offset_pass_start::lifts::fig8_start_sides_lift_only_with_a_named_reason`: now also asserts at most 0 lifts on Inside and 3 on Outside.\n- `offset_pass_start::lifts::fig8_outside_pass_links_keep_off_the_part_and_enter_on_cut_floor` (new, heavy lane): no pass link lifts over the part, and no \"plunged into material\" note.\n- `offset_pass_start::fig8_outside_offset_has_no_plunge_into_material` (from #3823): the `known-fail #3825` marker and the `// known-fail-assert` line are removed. It is now a plain heavy-lane pin, and it passes.\n- `flute_reach::a_ten_mm_flute_names_its_cause_before_the_rapid_findings`: now asserts at most 3 rapid findings.\n- Crossing and overcut: `fig8_start_sides_have_no_crossing`, `fig8_outside_offset_cuts_no_move_at_full_width` (21 points or fewer), and the `pass_start_levels::ring_links` shape masks (`assert_no_overcut`, `assert_no_crossing`) stay green.\n\n## Gates\n\nAll on the final head (`f5e3155dc`, origin/main with #3823, #3837 and #3822 merged in):\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 173 steps (motion lib, the motion and app suites of the gate map), each green.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --only`: `app heavy: offset_pass_start`, `app heavy: flute_reach`, `app heavy: pocket_pass_start` and `motion heavy: pass_start_levels`: each ok. On the head before #3837: `app heavy: known fail #2849 ...` stays red as expected.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test offset_pass_start --test flute_reach -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- New unit pin: `machining2d::ring_side::tests::the_side_tolerance_keeps_a_real_short_wall_and_drops_a_flat_sliver` (a 0.1 mm wall stretch 50 um off the start side stays a wall; a stretch 5 um off reads as the start side).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No test reaches the new edge-route branch of `ring_links::link` with a route that passes the proof. On fig8 and the box fixtures, the two ends of each failed link stand on different loops of the area, or the pass start stands in uncut stock. Each chord of a route uses the proven `chord_proof`, so the route cannot post a chord that the straight link would refuse.\n- No app window was opened. The private models in `testdata/models` were not used.\n\n## Overlap\n\n- #3748 deletes the `dead_end_ramp` block in `ladder_links::pass_link`. This PR does not touch that block. The PR that merges second merges `main` plainly.\n- #3822 (the ring-law predicate for the pocket and Adaptive): not touched.\n\nChangelog: 2D Offset \"Pass starts at\" Inside and Outside read the part wall as one wall where the stock edge is near it: on fig8 the tool no longer lifts across the part to two tiny wall stretches and plunges into material there, and the pass link tries a route along the edge of the area before it lifts.\n\nEffort: max (no escalation)\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/3824-pass-link-edge-route.md`\n\nFixes #3824\nFixes #3825\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
